{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "red-bank-api-v2",
    "name": "Red Bank API",
    "description": "Red Bank - Blood Donation Management Platform API.\n\nAuthentication flow:\n1. Call **Create Session** with a Firebase ID token (Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}). This sets httpOnly `accessToken` + `refreshToken` cookies.\n2. All cookie-session routes use those cookies automatically (Postman Cookie Jar).\n3. Mutations require an `X-CSRF-Token` header; the collection pre-request script fetches it automatically from `GET /api/auth/csrf`.\n\nVariables to set in the environment:\n- `baseUrl`: e.g. http://localhost:5000\n- `firebaseIdToken`: a current Firebase ID token for the user you are testing with",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const method = (pm.request.method || '').toUpperCase();",
          "if (!['GET', 'HEAD', 'OPTIONS'].includes(method)) {",
          "  const base = pm.variables.get('baseUrl');",
          "  if (base) {",
          "    pm.sendRequest({ url: base + '/api/auth/csrf', method: 'GET' }, (err, res) => {",
          "      if (!err && res.code === 200) {",
          "        const token = res.json()?.data?.csrfToken;",
          "        if (token) pm.request.headers.add({ key: 'X-CSRF-Token', value: token });",
          "      }",
          "    });",
          "  }",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
